(S) ADDITIVITY.
  F(n) = F(p) + F(n/p), p = least prime factor, all 2 <= n <= N: failures = 0
  F(p) = F(p-1) for all 664578 odd primes p <= N: failures = 0
  => F is completely additive on [1, N] (induction on the number of prime factors).
  Shapiro's form C(mk) = C(m) + C(k) + [m, k both even], 2*10^6 random pairs, mk < 10^7: failures = 0

