(L) ON THE 3-SMOOTH LATTICE.
  3-smooth x <= N: 190; failures of F = a+b, H = a+b (a>=1) / b+1 (a=0), and of the chain shape: 0
  totient chain of 36 = 2^2 3^2: 36 -> 12 -> 4 -> 2 -> 1   i.e. (2,2) -> (2,1) -> (2,0) -> (1,0) -> (0,0);  H(36) = 4 = 2 + 2
  sandwich on the lattice:  a log_3(2) + b = log_3 m  <=  a + b  <=  a + b log_2(3) = log_2 m.
  dictionary: sigma(n) = k + s = H(2^k 3^s) for 2 <= n <= 20000 (sigma = standard steps to drop,
    repo convention; H by explicit totient chain of the 3-smooth number): failures = 0
    dropping times that occur below 20000: [1, 3, 6, 8, 11, 13, 16, 19, 21, 24, 26, 29, 32, 34] ...  (= L1 norms of the staircase
    points (floor(s log2 3) + 1, s); OEIS A122437 gives this spectrum)

(I) INVARIANCE UNDER THE ODD COLLATZ STEP.  v = n + 1,  T(n) + 1 = 3 v / 2  (n odd).
  3x+1:  F(T(n)+1) = F(n+1) for all 3333333 odd n with T(n)+1 <= N: failures = 0
  3x-1:  F(T'(n)-1) = F(n-1), T'(n) = (3n-1)/2, all 3333332 odd n >= 3 in range: failures = 0
  5x+1:  F(3 T5(n) + 1) - F(3n + 1), T5(n) = (5n+1)/2, 666666 odd n: values = [1]   (always +1 = F(5) - F(2))
  odd primes q with F(q) = F(2) = 1: [3]  (F(q) = F(q-1) = 1 forces q - 1 = 2)
  n with F(n) = 1 below N: [2, 3]
  example n = 35: v = 36 = 2^2 3^2 -> 54 = 2 3^3 -> 81 = 3^4 (n: 35 -> 53 -> 80); F(v) = 4 throughout.

  at an EVEN step n -> n/2 the coordinate moves v -> (v+1)/2 and F is not conserved:
